  "text_md": "![](<af928f5861db3a8592e9cf2cc54ea819bd462606_page_1_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\nCERAWEEK\n\nagora\n\n# Houston; Texas\n\nMarch 9-13, 2020 | www.ceraweek.com  \n\n# Media Registration is Now Open for CERAWeek by IHS Markit 2020  \n\n  Applications for media registration can be submitted at the following link:   https://bit.ly/2LoeSGU  \n\nAll members of the media interested in attending CERAWeek 2020 are required to apply for accreditation.  \n\nComplete details related to media registration are included below in this email.  \n\n# About CERAWeek 2020  \n\nCERAWeek 2020 will kick off Monday, March 9 at the Hilton Americas-Houston.  \n\nCERAWeek by IHS Markit is the premier annual international gathering of energy industry leaders, experts, government officials and policymakers, leaders from the technology, financial and industrial communities – and energy technology innovators. Chaired by Daniel Yergin, CERAWeek 2020 will be the event’s 39th installment.  \n\nVisit www.ceraweek.com for the most up-to-date event information and follow us via @CERAWeek . Listed session times, topics and speakers are subject to change.    \n\n# Media Registration Details:  \n\nAll members of the media interested in attending CERAWeek 2020 are required to apply for accreditation.  \n\nJournalists should submit their request for media registration at the following link: https://bit.ly/2LoeSGU\n\nAs always, the CERAWeek Media Relations Team is happy to provide a designated media work room as part of our conference-wide efforts to make journalists’ experiences convenient and productive at the conference.  \n\n# CERAWeek 2020 Media Work Room Amenities:  \n\nFully-staffed Media Work Room adjacent to the CERAWeek Briefing Room  \n\n",
